.TH OLLAMA\-MESH-MODELS 1 "2026-08-17" "ollama-mesh dev" "ollama-mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
ollama\-mesh-models \- fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ollama\-mesh models
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pull <node> <model>
start pulling a model onto a node (async - does not wait for completion)
.TP
.B delete <node> <model>
delete a model from a node's local storage
.TP
.B unload <node> <model>
unload a model from a node's warm state
.TP
.B list <node>
list models present on a node's local storage (per\-node, not the fleet\-wide aggregate above)
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MESH_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MESH_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MESH_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBollama\-mesh\fR(1)
